<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Portuguese Angola</h1><p class="st-meta">1575 CE – 1975 CE · capital Luanda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Portugal's West African colony centred on Luanda, for three centuries the largest source of enslaved Africans shipped to Brazil.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1575 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paulo-dias-de-novais">Paulo Dias de Novais</a> arrived on the coast with a royal charter to conquer the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ndongo">Kingdom of Ndongo</a>, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> the following year. The colony grew from a coastal base through wars with Ndongo, alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imbangala">Imbangala</a> bands and the founding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benguela">Benguela</a> in 1617, always driven by the demand for slaves in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governors in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> relied on forts along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwanza-river">Kwanza</a>, African auxiliaries and trading fairs to obtain captives, and Luanda's merchants were closely tied to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> occupied Luanda from 1641 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-correia-de-sa-e-benevides">Salvador Correia de Sa</a> recaptured it in 1648. After the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> in the 19th century, Portugal pushed inland, and 20th-century settlers developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>, diamonds and later oil.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Nationalist revolt began in 1961, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpla">MPLA</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-of-angola">FNLA</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unita">UNITA</a> fighting Portugal. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution">Carnation Revolution</a> of 1974, Portugal withdrew, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> became independent on 11 November 1975 amid a civil war between the movements.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/portuguese-angola.jpg" alt="Portuguese Angola" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Columbano Bordalo Pinheiro Vector: Vítor Luís Rodrigues, António Martins-Tuválkin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Portugal_(official).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1575 CE – 1975 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Luanda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Paulo Dias de Novais, Salvador Correia de Sa, Francisco de Sousa Coutinho</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, traditional religions</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese, Kimbundu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Portuguese West Africa, Angola</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1775&amp;focus=portuguese-angola" aria-label="Portuguese Angola on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5046 2508 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Portuguese Angola lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5366 2764L5395 2668M5366 2764L5662 2807M5366 2764L5436 2888M5366 2764L5465 2895M5366 2764L5428 3067M5366 2764L4773 1044M5366 2764L5366 2764M5366 2764L5338 2642"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5395 2668h0M5662 2807h0M5436 2888h0M5465 2895h0M5428 3067h0M4773 1044h0M5366 2764h0M5338 2642h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5366 2764h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5366 2764h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Luanda. <a href="/atlas?year=1775&amp;focus=portuguese-angola">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
